  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday Night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1123 PM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThe SE CONUS ridge center will shift west and will be more\noverhead toward the end of the week. Before this occurs, CAMs\nsuggest one more day of low afternoon shower/storm chances mainly\nacross NW AR Thursday, before another hot and dry day Friday. The\nmulti-model ensemble means still show a front pushing into the \nregion late in this upcoming weekend into early next week with \nincreasing rain/storm chances. This will hopefully put an end to\nthe daily heat advisories for the summer.\n\nLacy",
